From: Lajosházi, László Gergely <lajoshazilg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pipeline: simple: carry the input stride request on multiplanar devices

The software ISP asks the capture device for an input stride its GPU can
import, by putting the number in planes[0].bpl of the V4L2DeviceFormat it
passes to setFormat(). On a single-planar device that arrives:
trySetFormatSingleplane() copies planes[0].bpl into the ioctl argument
unconditionally.

On a multiplanar one it does not. trySetFormatMultiplane() takes the plane
count from V4L2DeviceFormat::planesCount, which defaults to zero and is never
set here, and then copies bytesperline only for planes below that count - so
the request leaves as num_planes = 0 with no bytesperline at all, and the
driver answers with whatever the format needs. libcamera then reports the
driver as having ignored a request it was never shown.

Measured on a Fairphone 3, whose camss capture nodes are multiplanar: the
kernel grants a requested bytesperline of 2560 through a direct VIDIOC_TRY_FMT
and returns 2400 to libcamera for the same node in the same second. With the
plane count set, the two agree and the input buffer imports instead of being
uploaded a frame at a time.

Set it alongside the stride, and only where a stride is actually being asked
for, so nothing changes for a debayer that has no preference. One plane is the
right count here for the same reason the request is: the software ISP's input
is single-plane raw Bayer.

Signed-off-by: Lajosházi, László Gergely <lajoshazilg@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
---
 src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
+++ b/src/libcamera/pipeline/simple/simple.cpp
@@ -1545,7 +1545,11 @@ int SimplePipelineHandler::configure(Camera *camera, CameraConfiguration *c)
 	uint32_t requested_bpl = 0;
 	if (data->swIsp_)
 		requested_bpl = data->swIsp_->preferredInputStride(videoFormat.toPixelFormat(), pipeConfig->captureSize);
-	captureFormat.planes[0].bpl = requested_bpl;
+	if (requested_bpl) {
+		/* A multiplanar device copies bytesperline only for the planes it is told about. */
+		captureFormat.planesCount = 1;
+		captureFormat.planes[0].bpl = requested_bpl;
+	}

 	ret = video->setFormat(&captureFormat);
 	if (ret)
